    "locale_map": "toIntlLocale(app language) -> the locale every chart formatter uses (WP14 §1.6.4): underscores become hyphens; the aliases en -> en-US, hin -> hi, zh -> zh-CN and pt -> pt-BR apply; any other tag stays as it is; a tag the platform has no date data for (web: Intl.DateTimeFormat.supportedLocalesOf(tag) is empty or throws; desktop: !DateFormat.localeExists(tag) after initializeDateFormatting()) and the empty tag fall back to en-US. Rows are [{app, intl}].",
    "cases": "formatChartDateLabel(key, condition, locale, week_of_template) -> the label of a canonical chart date key (WP14 §1.6.5). condition is a DateConditionPB name. Day YYYY-MM-DD -> skeleton yMMMMd; Month YYYY-MM -> yMMM; Year YYYY -> y; Week (the Monday key YYYY-MM-DD) -> week_of_template with its two {} filled in order by the Monday as MMMd (yMMMd when the Sunday six days later is in another year) and the Sunday as yMMMd; Relative with a YYYY-MM key (a date beyond the relative buckets) -> as Month. rel:* keys are not formatted here: their labels are the translated board.dateCondition.* texts. Keys are read as calendar dates (no time zone), never parsed back from labels.",
    "skeletons": "web Intl.DateTimeFormat options: yMMMMd {year: numeric, month: long, day: numeric}, yMMM {year: numeric, month: short}, y {year: numeric}, MMMd {month: short, day: numeric}, yMMMd {year: numeric, month: short, day: numeric}; desktop DateFormat.yMMMMd, .yMMM, .y, .MMMd, .yMMMd with the locale.",
    "overrides": "{locale: {skeleton: CLDR pattern}}: when Chrome ICU and Dart intl disagree for a pinned locale, both clients format that skeleton with the pattern instead (pattern letters y, M, MMM, MMMM, d, quoted literals). Empty: when this file was generated, Chrome 145 (V8 ICU), Node 23 (ICU 76.1, CLDR 46) and Dart intl 0.20.2 produced the same text for every case."
